From 2981e3a215243d5f1575877c3e34ae805fbfddd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude-sandbox <sandbox@local>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 10:23:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] scrobble: extract a WatchScrobbleSink interface for the
 player fan-out

Two real scrobble sinks now exist, and the three playback-event fan-outs
named both services explicitly - six near-identical launch blocks whose
only difference was the service and the log prefix. Extract the shape
they share and iterate over a list instead.

Behaviourally inert by construction: the same coroutineScope for start,
the same separate NonCancellable launches for stop, the same runCatching
isolation, and log messages built from a sink name that reproduces the
previous strings verbatim. No DI change - a plain list keeps the wiring
visible at the point of use.

Not converted: the external-player return path in StreamScreenViewModel
and ExternalPlaybackTracker, which scrobbles to Trakt and sends nothing
to MDBList. That gap predates this change and is left in place because
it cannot be exercised on an in-app playback setup; routing those two
sites through this interface is the fix once someone can verify it. The
interface KDoc records this so it reads as a decision, not an oversight.

Upstream: NuvioMedia/NuvioTV.
